{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\text{d}_{X/S}$", "MATH_0002": "$i$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{d}_{X/S} : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}^2 \\subset \\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2 \\to \\Omega_{X/S}/\\mathcal{I}\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_X/\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \\to i^*\\Omega_{X/S}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-differential-seq}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-i-star-equivalence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9fa49f12dcd5a3860ff7fc002f61d42bdcf85d41d8d4fa6afe583e57a24d2ea5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0baca1019c98118cca3cba7cfad20d2fc64fbccd38e66b50c8a0a554afd8fed2", "source_text": "This is the sheafified version of\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>. However\nwe should make sure we can define the first arrow globally.\nHence we explain the meaning of ``induced by <MATH_0001>'' here.\nNamely, we may assume that <MATH_0002> is a closed immersion by\nshrinking <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe the sheaf of ideals corresponding to <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006>\nmaps the subsheaf <MATH_0007> to\n<MATH_0008>. Hence it induces a map\n<MATH_0009>\nwhich is <MATH_0010>-linear.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002> this corresponds to a map\n<MATH_0011> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be15b260ef29fa87ec9c7c0262ba421e944942bd1aff5345bf35a12cb2342b0d", "unit_id": "tag:01UZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \\to i^*\\Omega_{X/S} \\to \\Omega_{Z/S} \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$s : S \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}_{S/X} \\to s^*\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\text{d}_{X/S}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-differentials-relative-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-differentials-relative-immersion-section}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8103e1aad08764d84423dc9b9d189014f7073d802aa7782714af86701e8f02cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3a3133dbc8d66f99d29ae769b970ddec6cdf33c8863fbc12076de8999177f8d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an immersion of schemes over <MATH_0002>, and\nassume <MATH_0003> (locally) has a left inverse. Then the canonical\nsequence\n<MATH_0004>\nof\nLemma <REF_0001>\nis (locally) split exact. In particular, if <MATH_0005> is a section\nof the structure morphism <MATH_0006> then the map\n<MATH_0007> induced by\n<MATH_0008> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:baa9aa82fb97c323209fd1e2da6e2fefa90310244d527f2b791bb2affdfd591a", "unit_id": "tag:0474:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X, Z, S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : X \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$i^*c_g$", "MATH_0005": "$i^*\\Omega_{X/S} \\to \\Omega_{Z/S}$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "MATH_0007": "$s : Z = S \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Omega_{Z/S} = 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-differential-seq-split}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{modules-lemma-check-functoriality-differentials}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{homology-lemma-ses-split}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-section-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0b7666836bcf117b424da3455541d7d79a75c0f6bbe8d9da416b52f0348ae710", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bcc3f6702e4d2b61ebf7c0162acb39e43761b66f6a3131fca6a52f2bfd3d60d8", "source_text": "It follows from Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthat the result holds when <MATH_0001> are affine. In general we conclude\nthe sequence is locally split exact. If <MATH_0002> is a left inverse\nof <MATH_0003>, then <MATH_0004> is a right inverse of the map\n<MATH_0005> by\nModules, Lemma <REF_0002>. \nThis implies the sequence is split by\nHomology, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nFinally, if <MATH_0006> is a section, then it is an immersion <MATH_0007>\nover <MATH_0008> (see Schemes, Lemma <REF_0004>)\nand in that case <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0188cc2ce669c19324d48ebb64f478a4ff4f7963e77a559102e62dfb6dd32571", "unit_id": "tag:0474:proof"}
